y from the  modern world which they see as dangerous  this is a chance for people to start  fresh somewhere without the violence and  the madness we briefly see lila check  her instagram feed where she supports  various social justice issues this one  says stop racism a nod to black lives  matter and this one's about gun control  you'll notice the hashtag stonebrook  strong the high school where the  shooting happened its name is very  similar to stoneman douglas high school  which saw one of the most recent and  tragic school shootings in u.s history  it's ironic then that guns were the  thing that almost killed her in the  school shooting yet will be the thing  that saves her in the end so i wasn't  quite sure what the filmmakers were  trying to say here further confusion is  added when lila tells her sister melody  that she doesn't want to move here  because she'll miss her friends one i  thought they died in a school shooting  and two does she really want to go back  to the high school where she saw all her  friends massacred anyways that's besides  the point i will say the foreshadowing  dialogue in the first hour is chef's  kiss yes but we have a vision for this  place all it needs is young blood wish i  now know i would come  i'd put my face on she literally gets  her face ripped off this is the harlow  orphanage a place that's implied  leatherface grew up this photo here was  taken in 1975 two years after the events  of the original film it's heavily  implied that virginia here is  leatherface's mother both her and one of  the officers refers to him as her boy  although this might be a name used to  describe all the boys at the orphanage  leatherface being her last one who never  found a home if it is indeed her  biological child she has never seen in  the original film but if it's one she  brought into her orphanage it would  suggest leatherface found adoption from  his crazy uncle and brother after the  events in 1973.  bonus points if you caught this imag